Subject: Volunteer Yurt/Cabin Host Position at Umpqua Lighthouse State Park

Dear Franki Allegra,

I hope this message finds you well. My name is Robert Samuel White (Sam), a=
nd I was recently encouraged to apply for a volunteer host position within =
Oregon State Parks by Matt, a host at Cape Blanco, and Jerry, a park ranger=
 I've come to know at both Cape Blanco and Humbug Mountain State Parks. Bot=
h have spoken positively about my time here and expressed their willingness=
 to vouch for me as a strong candidate.

Over the past two months, I've been living and engaging deeply with the sou=
thern Oregon coast, where I feel a profound sense of belonging. After a mon=
th-long journey from Kentucky, I arrived here and knew almost immediately I=
 was "home." I've been exploring this landscape-its lighthouses, rugged bea=
ches, and trails-with reverence and a strong desire to contribute meaningfu=
lly to its preservation and maintenance. I'm committed to staying along the=
 101 for the long term and would be honored to support Oregon's State Parks=
 through volunteer service.

The Yurt/Cabin Host position at Umpqua Lighthouse State Park aligns perfect=
ly with my skills, strengths, and current way of life. I am deeply organize=
d, hardworking, and accustomed to the physical tasks required, such as clea=
ning, light landscaping, and general maintenance. I also value providing ex=
cellent visitor experiences and creating welcoming, well-kept spaces for al=
l who come to enjoy these parks. I am fully capable of meeting the role's r=
equirements and bring with me not only practical skills but a personal conn=
ection to the parks I would serve.

If you have time for a conversation, I'd greatly appreciate the opportunity=
 to discuss this position and learn more about the expectations and applica=
tion process. I currently have limited internet access while camped at Humb=
ug Mountain, but I can find connectivity for any necessary next steps.

Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibilit=
y of contributing to the incredible work being done across Oregon State Par=
ks. Please feel free to reach out via email or phone at your earliest conve=
nience.

Warm regards,
Robert Samuel White
828-333-8877
rsw@rswfire.com<mailto:rsw@rswfire.com>

